{"core": "Wisdom sits with what is not yet understood and waits for the shape beneath things to surface. In Abstraction, it works on the mind's pull toward pure pattern — the place where thinking untethers from anything it can touch. Overdone, the waiting deepens the untethering: Wisdom holds so still inside a structure with no floor that the knowing never lands anywhere. Patterns accumulate; nothing closes.", "sheetLine": "The depth kept deepening until there was nowhere left to stand."}
